<article class="env-lemma" id="0FDF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FDF">Lemma <span data-tag="0FDF">36.38.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Noetherian scheme. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  K_0(\textit{Coh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)) = K_0(D^ b(\textit{Coh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)) = K_0(D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X))  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first equality is Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FCP" data-tag="0FCP">13.28.2</a>. We have $K_0(\textit{Coh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)) = K_0(D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X))$ by Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FCS" data-tag="0FCS">13.28.5</a>. This proves the lemma. (We can also use that $D^ b(\textit{Coh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)) = D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ by Proposition <a href="/tag/0FDB" data-tag="0FDB">36.11.2</a> to see the second equality.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>